// ═══ CAS MECHANISM ═══
// Hardware instruction (single CPU cycle, uninterruptible):
// boolean CAS(memoryAddress, expectedValue, newValue):
//   if memory[address] == expected:
//     memory[address] = newValue
//     return true
//   else:
//     return false  // another thread changed it!

// ═══ HOW AtomicInteger USES CAS ═══
// AtomicInteger.incrementAndGet():
public int incrementAndGet() {
    int prev, next;
    do {
        prev = get();           // volatile read: current value
        next = prev + 1;        // compute new value
    } while (!compareAndSet(prev, next));  // CAS: try to write!
    // If CAS fails: another thread changed prev → loop retries with fresh value!
    return next;
}
// compareAndSet: calls Unsafe.compareAndSwapInt → CPU CMPXCHG instruction!

// ═══ LOW CONTENTION: CAS succeeds first try → fast! ═══
// 2 threads, rarely collide:
// Thread-1: CAS(99→100) (Recommended) → done in 1 attempt!
// Thread-2: CAS(99→100) → retry → CAS(100→101) (Recommended) → 2 attempts

// ═══ HIGH CONTENTION: CAS retries many times → slow! ═══
// 100 threads all CAS-ing the same AtomicLong:
// Thread-1: CAS(99→100) (Recommended) 
// Thread-2 through Thread-100: CAS(99→100) → retry → CAS(100→101) → ...
// Each thread retries ~50 times on average!
// 100 threads × 50 retries = 5000 wasted CAS attempts!
// CPU: spinning at 100% doing nothing useful!

// ═══ THE ABA PROBLEM ═══
// Thread-1: reads value A
// Thread-2: changes A → B → A (back to A!)
// Thread-1: CAS(A → C) → succeeds! But value was modified and restored!
// For most counters: not a problem (just a number)
// For linked lists/stacks: ABA can cause corruption!
// Fix: AtomicStampedReference — CAS on (value + version stamp)!

AtomicStampedReference<String> ref = new AtomicStampedReference<>("A", 0);
int[] stamp = new int[1];
String val = ref.get(stamp);  // val="A", stamp[0]=0
ref.compareAndSet("A", "C", 0, 1);  // checks BOTH value AND stamp!
// If another thread changed A→B→A, stamp is now 2 (not 0) → CAS fails!

// ═══ FIXES FOR HIGH-CONTENTION CAS SPINNING ═══
// 1. LongAdder: striped cells → each thread CAS-es own cell → zero contention!
// 2. Exponential backoff: Thread.sleep(random * 2^attempt) between retries
// 3. Eliminate shared state: ThreadLocal, immutable objects
// 4. Coarsen: batch updates, reduce CAS frequency
